&lt;p&gt;To close this pull request, make a commit to your master/trunk branch&lt;br/&gt;
with (at least) the following in the commit message:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    This closes #2688&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;commit 6a95a845056e7d509ad3fcf78738f1d59f7cc892&lt;br/&gt;
Author: Alexander Paschenko &amp;lt;alexander.a.paschenko@gmail.com&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Date:   2017-09-18T18:04:57Z&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6403&quot; title=&quot;IgniteSqlNotNullConstraintTest.testTransactionalAddColumnNotNullCheckDmlInsertValues fails periodically&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6403&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6403&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; SchemaOperationManager always waits for node that has initiated operation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16170480" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 18 Sep 2017 18:44:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=al.psc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;al.psc&quot;&gt;al.psc&lt;/a&gt;, the fix is incorrect, unfortunately. Please change target test as follows to see that it still fails:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void testTransactionalAddColumnNotNullCheckDmlInsertValues() &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception {
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;) {
            checkAddColumnNotNullCheckDmlInsertValues(CacheAtomicityMode.TRANSACTIONAL);

            afterTest();
            beforeTest();
        }
    }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16170484" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 18 Sep 2017 18:47:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=al.psc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;al.psc&quot;&gt;al.psc&lt;/a&gt;, root cause of the problem is that client nodes receive custom discovery messages asynchronously. For this reason server node may complete operations and notify the client before changes are appled to client schema. As a result, we complete operations before local H2 is ready. To fix the problem we should do the following:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Client future must consist of two parts - server part and local part.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Server part is completed in the same way it is implemented now.&lt;br/&gt;
3) Client part is completed when changes are applied on the client.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16170498" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 18 Sep 2017 18:58:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=al.psc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;al.psc&quot;&gt;al.psc&lt;/a&gt;, please disregard my previous message, it is wrong. As far as I see we complete client future when &lt;tt&gt;SchemaFinishDiscoveryMessage&lt;/tt&gt; is received. At this point all necessary changes should alread by applied to the client as message ordering is guaranteed, and se should have received relevant &lt;tt&gt;SchemaProposeDiscoveryMessage&lt;/tt&gt; at this point.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
